message: If you use these materials, please cite them as below.
title: "Viscosity Measurement Laboratory: Interactive Falling Ball, Saybolt, and Rotary Viscometers with Laboratory Materials"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based, offline-capable laboratory covering three methods of viscosity
  measurement: a falling ball viscometer in which the sphere falls at the velocity
  the student's own timings imply, a Saybolt viscometer that drains over the
  student's own efflux time, and a rotary viscometer station that plots the
  student's temperature sweep. The Reynolds number is computed live and the
  validity of Stokes' law is labelled rather than hidden, so students can see a
  model return a repeatable number outside the conditions it was derived for.
  Includes a student handout, an instructor answer sheet with live calculation,
  a grading tool that computes every answer both from master and from reported
  measurements, and verification suites covering the physics, the unit
  conversions, and the interface behaviour.
